{"nodes": [{"id": "reportingblueprint_doc", "label": "Istifadah Reporting Blueprint", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_six_tags_model", "label": "Six-tag entry grain + line-item level", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every entry is tagged on six independent axes (department, admin head, zone, budget head/category, vendor, entry type) plus a line-item level beneath it; almost every report in the catalogue is a measure crossed with one or two of these tags, and the line-item level is what lets rates compare across vendors and time."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_family_a", "label": "Report Family A \u2014 Budget & spend", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What is missing is not totals but comparison \u2014 against budget over time, against pace, against last year, against each other."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_family_b", "label": "Report Family B \u2014 Vendors", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vendor alias-merging and normalization make concentration, dependency and relationship analysis actually work rather than fragmenting across spelling variants."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_family_c", "label": "Report Family C \u2014 What we bought", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The line-item family is the part no conventional expense report can produce, because a rate is comparable in a way an invoice total never is."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_family_d", "label": "Report Family D \u2014 Entry integrity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The controls already run and attach rupees to what they find; missing is the reporting layer turning 23 exception types and 14 flag types into a short actionable list."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_family_e", "label": "Report Family E \u2014 Executive framings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No new data \u2014 arranges existing measures into shapes a decision-maker can act on in under a minute."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_concentration_curve", "label": "B-01 Concentration curve (flagship)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately not a classic dual-axis Pareto chart, since two scales on one chart is the most common way a finance chart misleads."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_above_median_overpayment", "label": "C-04 Above-median overpayment (flagship)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "(rate - median) x quantity, summed, produces a headline rupee figure benchmarked against the organization's own purchase history rather than an external one, very hard to argue with."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_exception_heat_map", "label": "D-01 Exception heat map (flagship)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sequential single-hue shading, never a rainbow, so darker always and only means more rupees at risk."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_purchase_tree", "label": "C-02 Purchase tree (flagship)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Item family to catalogue item to vendor to specific bills, drillable at every level \u2014 the only view answering 'what did we actually buy'."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_instrument_type_mix", "label": "C-09 Instrument-type mix (flagship)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Turns a compliance question (tax invoice vs letterhead bill vs cash memo) into a money question measured in rupees, not counts."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_department_league_table", "label": "E-01 Department league table (flagship)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ranking departments on budget adherence, projected landing, spend share, documentation coverage and rupees at risk changes behaviour in a way that reporting totals never does."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_executive_brief_screen", "label": "Executive Brief screen design", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Composed to read top-to-bottom as an argument: position, what moved, where to look, what needs a decision \u2014 for trustees and senior administration in under thirty seconds."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_present_mode", "label": "Present mode feature", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A full-screen, large-type, no-navigation rendering of the Brief for a projector \u2014 a stylesheet and a keyboard shortcut that is the difference between a web app and a presented report."}, {"id": "reportingblueprint_board_pack", "label": "Board pack (PDF + workbook) concept", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Executive Brief rendered to a scheduled PDF and matching workbook, in the spreadsheet idiom the organisation already circulates widely."}], "edges": [{"source": "reportingblueprint_doc", "target": "reportingblueprint_six_tags_model", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "reportingblueprint_six_tags_model", "target": "reportingblueprint_family_a", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "reportingblueprint_six_tags_model", "target": "reportingblueprint_family_b", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "reportingblueprint_six_tags_model", "target": "reportingblueprint_family_c", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reporting-blueprint.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "reportingblueprint_six_tags_model", 